        <item>
            <title>1.3.32</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:33:04 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>10332</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.32</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 1.3.32</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Codex connects on Windows. The Codex app for Windows does not come with a command line tool MotionUI can run, so Connect failed with "could not find the Codex tools". MotionUI now adds its tools to the Codex settings file directly, which the Codex app, the Codex CLI and the editor extensions all read.</li>
  <li>After Effects panel 1.6.12: Connect now in the AI tab does the same for Codex, and uses the Node.js runtime of the MotionUI app, so it no longer asks you to install Node.js.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
